{"title":"2017 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 5","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The sum of two nonzero real numbers is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> times their product. What is the sum of the reciprocals of the two numbers?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/1/571c1026e49506d70e6e271bdb9920253b289b54.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 1\\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 2\\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 4\\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 8\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"357\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let the two real numbers be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/4/b6400c6fe3f1ed70e5afd387a9686cdc3fa09531.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x,y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"27\" height=\"11\" />. We are given that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/9/7b9912f427d0dfacd861d2641c7b4eeaea8ea46a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x+y=4xy,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"99\" height=\"15\" /> and dividing both sides by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/7/3f79c3676b62fb47243e0d357c87115b6f3395e4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$xy$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"22\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/b/b4b2ccfe02561ef15a393ba4e97058998006e2a9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{x}{xy}+\\frac{y}{xy}=4.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"107\" height=\"36\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/1/ea1dadbf53587b5968e46e59c6f61f87125eeed4.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{1}{y}+\\frac{1}{x}=\\boxed{\\textbf{(C) } 4}.\\]\" width=\"131\" height=\"40\" />\n</p><p>Note: we can easily verify that this is the correct answer; for example, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/e/5fe5e71c7d8317d4177fa56b61211bcca007e682.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(\\frac{1}{2}, \\frac{1}{2}\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"57\" height=\"43\" /> works, and the sum of their reciprocals is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Instead of using algebra, another approach at this problem would be to notice the fact that one of the nonzero numbers has to be a fraction.\nSee for yourself. And by looking into fractions, we immediately see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/1/4e1965f8d70832ded66434c75a7bd52b75090af0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> would fit the rule. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/1/c614e06fc27d91fdb119a3ea4a8a05bce31942b5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(C)} 4}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"52\" height=\"28\" />\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Notice that from the information given above, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/8/d08c1d599ed5c382ab7827339699084d0ead73e5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x+y=4xy$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"95\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p>Because the sum of the reciprocals of two numbers is just the sum of the two numbers over the product of the two numbers or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/b/3abd2341c3a6904f4b8f972cf00c466568ef1190.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{x+y}{xy}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"44\" height=\"39\" /> \n</p><p>We can solve this by substituting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/8/898ebd560e26a7b4e81a23951a3d3a678e15aa56.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x+y\\implies 4xy$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"120\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>Our answer is simply <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/d/45d5c09e0ebaed53108dba7ea9b8b3a6fcd86265.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{4xy}{xy}\\implies4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"91\" height=\"40\" />.\n</p><p>Therefore, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/c/88cfe513eb8c018f4f918d63b4f244a861f9558a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(C) } 4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"55\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_1\">Video Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/str7kmcRMY8\">https://youtu.be/str7kmcRMY8</a>\n</p><p>(TheBeautyofMath)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_2\">Video Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/TooKNMK3slY\">https://youtu.be/TooKNMK3slY</a>\n</p><p>~savannahsolver\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10A\" title=\"2017 AMC 10A\">2017 AMC 10A</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10A_Problems\" title=\"2017 AMC 10A Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10A_Answer_Key\" title=\"2017 AMC 10A Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2017 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 4\">Problem 4</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2017 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 6\">Problem 6</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2017 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wi